WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.654
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:08.038
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.338 --> 00:00:15.019
Unit nine: Consumer Society. In this unit, you will discuss shopping habits, advertising and services.

4
00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:17.006
consumerism.

5
00:00:17.706 --> 00:00:21.401
consumerism means a culture focused on buying lots of things.

6
00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.525
Consumerism encourages us to buy more than we need.

7
00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.494
Your turn. Say: consumerism.

8
00:00:30.194 --> 00:00:31.253
consumerism.

9
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.402
materialistic.

10
00:00:34.102 --> 00:00:37.518
materialistic means caring too much about money and possessions.

11
00:00:37.818 --> 00:00:40.584
He's become very materialistic since getting rich.

12
00:00:41.284 --> 00:00:43.843
Your turn. Say: materialistic.

13
00:00:46.543 --> 00:00:47.893
materialistic.

14
00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:49.954
brand loyalty.

15
00:00:50.654 --> 00:00:53.582
brand loyalty means always buying from the same company.

16
00:00:53.882 --> 00:00:55.801
Apple has strong brand loyalty.

17
00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:59.281
Your turn. Say: brand loyalty.

18
00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:03.168
brand loyalty.

19
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:05.707
advertising campaign.

20
00:01:06.407 --> 00:01:10.160
advertising campaign means a series of advertisements with one goal.

21
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.947
The advertising campaign doubled sales.

22
00:01:13.647 --> 00:01:16.287
Your turn. Say: advertising campaign.

23
00:01:18.987 --> 00:01:20.534
advertising campaign.

24
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.714
target audience.

25
00:01:23.414 --> 00:01:26.667
target audience means the group of people a product is aimed at.

26
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:29.489
Teenagers are the target audience for this game.

27
00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.818
Your turn. Say: target audience.

28
00:01:35.518 --> 00:01:36.879
target audience.

29
00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:38.896
fast fashion.

30
00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:43.337
fast fashion means cheap clothes made quickly to follow trends.

31
00:01:43.637 --> 00:01:45.880
Fast fashion creates a lot of waste.

32
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.105
Your turn. Say: fast fashion.

33
00:01:51.805 --> 00:01:53.062
fast fashion.

34
00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.527
planned obsolescence.

35
00:01:56.227 --> 00:02:00.676
planned obsolescence means designing products to stop working after a short time.

36
00:02:00.976 --> 00:02:03.429
Some phones are accused of planned obsolescence.

37
00:02:04.129 --> 00:02:07.071
Your turn. Say: planned obsolescence.

38
00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:11.283
planned obsolescence.

39
00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:13.354
bargain hunting.

40
00:02:14.054 --> 00:02:17.249
bargain hunting means looking for things at very low prices.

41
00:02:17.549 --> 00:02:19.723
My mum loves bargain hunting at the market.

42
00:02:20.423 --> 00:02:23.250
Your turn. Say: bargain hunting.

43
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.206
bargain hunting.

44
00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:30.251
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:30.551 --> 00:02:33.294
I had my phone repaired instead of buying a new one.

46
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:38.292
Smart. Some companies are accused of planned obsolescence.

47
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:44.012
Exactly. Advertising campaigns make us feel we need the latest model.

48
00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:49.792
Consumerism is everywhere. Even fast fashion is designed to be replaced.

49
00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:55.071
I'm trying to be less materialistic. I'm getting my old jacket altered.

50
00:02:56.383 --> 00:03:00.069
Good for you! And bargain hunting for second-hand items helps too.

51
00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:03.673
Grammar focus: Causative (advanced).

52
00:03:03.973 --> 00:03:08.504
Use have or get, plus object, plus past participle when a service is done for you.

53
00:03:08.804 --> 00:03:15.366
Use have plus person plus verb, or get plus person plus to plus verb, when you arrange or persuade someone.

54
00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:19.978
For example: I had my phone repaired. I got my brother to fix my bike.

55
00:03:20.278 --> 00:03:25.796
Have someone do = arrange for them to do it; get someone to do = persuade them to do it.

56
00:03:26.783 --> 00:03:29.738
Now read and listen. Buy Less, Choose Better.

57
00:03:30.038 --> 00:03:33.721
Modern consumerism encourages us to buy new things constantly.

58
00:03:35.017 --> 00:03:38.572
Advertising campaigns are carefully designed for each target audience.

59
00:03:39.883 --> 00:03:44.042
Fast fashion and planned obsolescence mean products don't last long.

60
00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.439
A growing number of people now have old items repaired instead of replacing them.

61
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.514
Choosing quality over quantity saves money and protects the environment.

62
00:03:55.817 --> 00:03:58.272
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:58.572 --> 00:04:01.059
Always buying from the same company is blank.

64
00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:05.453
A, brand loyalty. B, consumerism. C, fast fashion.

65
00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.705
The answer is A: brand loyalty.

66
00:04:13.217 --> 00:04:14.903
I need to get my car blank.

67
00:04:15.203 --> 00:04:18.531
A, service. B, serviced. C, to service.

68
00:04:22.517 --> 00:04:24.609
The answer is B: serviced.

69
00:04:26.117 --> 00:04:27.942
She had the mechanic blank the brakes.

70
00:04:28.242 --> 00:04:31.292
A, check. B, to check. C, checked.

71
00:04:35.283 --> 00:04:36.935
The answer is A: check.

72
00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.972
Caring too much about money and possessions is blank.

73
00:04:41.272 --> 00:04:45.227
A, materialistic. B, bargain hunting. C, target audience.

74
00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:51.878
The answer is A: materialistic.

75
00:04:53.383 --> 00:04:57.554
According to the text, what are more people doing instead of replacing items?

76
00:04:57.854 --> 00:05:01.798
A, throwing them away. B, having them repaired. C, selling them.

77
00:05:05.783 --> 00:05:08.189
The answer is B: having them repaired.

78
00:05:09.683 --> 00:05:13.729
Now it's your turn to speak. Do you think advertising influences what you buy?

79
00:05:19.029 --> 00:05:24.909
Definitely. I often have to stop myself from buying things I see in online advertising campaigns.

80
00:05:25.209 --> 00:05:26.814
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:27.817 --> 00:05:31.491
Great work today! You learned eight new words and causative (advanced).

82
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:35.546
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

83
00:05:35.846 --> 00:05:38.069
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

84
00:05:38.369 --> 00:05:40.998
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

